; DEPRECATED / DEAD FILE -- do not copy this into the Godot project.
;
; This .gdip file is NOT used. Confirmed by inspecting the shipped Godot
; 4.7.2 editor binary directly (strings + symbol table): the only
; "Invalid plugin config file" error string in that binary belongs to
; platform/android/export/export_plugin.cpp (the Android plugin loader).
; There is no .gdip / iOS-plugin-config parser anywhere in Godot 4.7 --
; the legacy Godot 3.x "iOS plugin" system (res://ios/plugins/*.gdip) does
; not exist in this engine version. An export attempt that places this file
; under res://ios/plugins/LittleBuddySpeech/ will not link Speech.framework
; or AVFoundation.framework, no matter how the [config]/[dependencies]
; sections are worded.
;
; The real mechanism in Godot 4.7 for injecting iOS system framework links
; is EditorExportPlugin.add_ios_framework(), called from a GDScript
; EditorPlugin's _export_begin(). See:
;   ios/speech_plugin/godot_project_overlay/addons/little_buddy_speech_export/
; for the addon that replaces this file, and README.md "Why not .gdip" for
; the full writeup of how this was confirmed (not guessed).
;
; This file is kept only as a paper trail of what was tried and ruled out.
